{"type":"thinking","text":"Interesting — the card is showing! \"WORLD 1-1\", lives x3. So after reset and Start,Start, we got the card (not the level). That means the title's Start→Start sequence showed the card? Hmm, actually after reset, pressing Start once goes to the 1-player game start which shows the \"WORLD 1-1\" card then the level. So the card appears at game start too!\n\nWait, my play_input was Start(6), none(60), Start(6), none(60). The first Start at the title begins the game (maybe it played the attract demo first?), the second Start... The card is showing now. Hmm, the card appeared and stayed because the emulator paused at the end of the run? No — the run ended paused, and the card happens to be showing.\n\nActually the card is transient; the run ended at frame 132, and the card is showing. So at game start, the card is displayed before 1-1. Interesting.\n\nBut wait — the HUD shows MARIO 000000, coin x00, WORLD 1-1, card \"WORLD 1-1\", lives x3. So this is the game-start card (a new game with 3 lives → $075A=2, card shows 3).\n\nNow I'm on the card with $0760=1 and $075C=1 written. When this card finishes, the level loads. Will it load 1-2? Let's find out! The card is paused. Let me resume a bit: play_input [] 120 from paused, then screenshot.\n\nBut note: the card at game start might have been drawn before my writes, and the level init may have already computed the area. Hmm. But the card is displayed BEFORE the level loads (it's the \"WORLD 1-1\" intro card). The level data is loaded during the card or after? In SMB1, the \"WORLD 1-1\" card is displayed, then the level loads. So writing $0760 now might be too late again (level data may load after the card).\n\nLet me just run and see.\n\nActually wait — this is the game-start card, and my earlier death card was the same kind. The card at game start is the \"world intro\" card. The game shows it and then the level. If the area selection happens when the card ENDS, then my $0760 write will take effect!\n\nHmm, but earlier when I was on the death card and wrote $075C=1, the level loaded 1-1. But I wrote $075C, not $0760. Now, at THIS card, I wrote $0760=1 and $075C=1. Let me run and see.\n\nLet me play_input [] 120 and screenshot.\n\nActually, I want to also confirm whether the game reads $0760 at card end. Let's see.\n\nNote: the card screenshot shows \"1-1\" because $075C... wait, $075F=0, $075C=1 would show \"1-2\". But the card shows \"1-1\"! So the card was drawn BEFORE my write (it shows the pre-write value 0). So my write happened after the card was drawn. If the level init already ran (and the area latched) before the card, then my $0760 write won't matter. Hmm.\n\nActually, in SMB1, the sequence is: level data loads (area selection + parsing), THEN the \"WORLD 1-1\" card is drawn while the level finishes loading, then gameplay. So the area was likely latched before the card was displayed. That would explain why writing world/level on the card doesn't change the level.\n\nSo to change the level, I must write $0760 BEFORE the area selection — i.e., before the card appears, ideally before the level-init state machine runs. At game start, the area selection happens right when Start begins. Writing on the title screen wouldn't survive the new-game init.\n\nHmm. So the only reliable way is: die, and during the death sequence (before the reload's area selection) set $0760. The death sequence: Mario dies → death animation (~2s) → then the card/level init. If I write $0760 during the death animation (before the level init), it should take.\n\nBut timing is hard.\n\nAlternative: reach 1-2 legitimately (flagpole). \n\nAlternative: use the trace to find when $074E is written on reload, then write $0760 just before.\n\nAlternative: The area selection routine $9C00 uses $075F/$0760. If I can find where it's called and force a call... too deep.\n\nHmm, what about this: The death reload might re-run the level-init state machine, which calls $9C00 at some step. If I set