vel-init which is at the death (before the animation). Hmm.\n\nOK, let me reconsider legitimate play. Maybe I can just beat 1-1 with a good input script. Let me think about 1-1's obstacles:\n- First Goomba at x~290.\n- Pipes at x~700-1000, 1500, etc.\n- Gaps? 1-1 has no pits until? Actually 1-1 has no bottomless pits. The main hazards are Goombas and pipes (you bump into them and stop, but no death). Actually pipes just block; you must jump over them. Koopa Troopas later.\n- Wait, 1-1 does have a pit? No, I think 1-1's ground is continuous except near the end there's a gap before the staircase? Hmm, 1-1 has no pits except maybe none. Actually the level is mostly flat with pipes; you can just hold Right and jump over pipes/Goombas.\n\nA script: hold Right, and press A periodically (e.g., jump every 30 frames). Jumping over pipes: you need to jump when near a pipe. Periodic jumps might work: if you jump every ~20-25 frames while holding right, you'd clear most obstacles. Let me try a script: [{buttons:[\"right\",\"a\"],frames:X},{buttons:[\"right\"],frames:Y}] repeated. But jumping too often is fine; landing on the ground and jumping again.\n\nHmm, but Goombas: jumping over them works if timed. Periodic jumps might land on a Goomba.\n\nAlternatively, use the famous \"hold right + A\" and hope. SMB1 1-1 speedrun is ~35s; with periodic jumps maybe.\n\nActually, there might be an easier trick: disable enemies! The mapping shows how: write prgRom enemy list terminator, or set enemy slots. But enemy writes are ROM (ledgered) — we don't want to alter the ROM for a scene mapping. We could write RAM: set $0016 (enemy type) to something harmless, or set $000F (enemy flag) to 0 to despawn. But the spawner re-spawns as Mario advances.\n\nBetter: write the enemy list pointer $E9/$EA to point at an empty list ($9F00 has $FF end marker per the mapping!). The mapping note: \"ledgered write_memory prgRom 0x1CEF 0x01->0x00 pointed 1-1 at the $FF end-marker at $9F00 (live $E9/$EA=$9F00