{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_2TGezTnq9mUfOxQrghpn1886","tool":"record_mapping","input":{"mapping_type":"address","id":"0x0760","name":"level/area index that selects which area the game loads","format":"binary (index added to the world base table $9CB4)","notes":"This is how the game picks the area it loads, proven in the emulator. The level-init area selector at CPU $9C00-$9C12 (prgRom 0x1C00) does JSR $9C13, where $9C13: LDY $075F (world) / LDA $9CB4,Y (world base table = 0,5,10,14,19,23,27,32 for worlds 1-8) / CLC / ADC $0760 / TAY / LDA $9CBC,Y (level-header table) / RTS. The returned header is stored to $0750 at $9C06; then $9C09-$9C0F derives the palette group with (header & $60) << 1 as a 4x ROL, storing $074E, and LoadAreaData ($9C22-$9C2E) sets $074F = header & $1F. The layout pointer is $9D28[$074E] + $074F indexing the low/high tables $9D2C/$9D4E; the enemy pointer is $9CE0[$074E] + $074F indexing $9CE4/$9D06. For World 1 ($075F=0, base 0) the header index = $0760: index 0 -> header $25 -> $074E=1, $074F=5 -> World 1-1 (layout $A68E); index 2 -> header $C0 -> $074E=2 (underground), $074F=0 -> World 1-2 (layout header $AC35, records $AC37). $074E selects the palette block through $85BB = $01,$02,$03,$04: $074E=0 -> selector 1 $8CA4, 1 -> selector 2 $8CC8 (overworld), 2 -> selector 3 $8CEC (underground, black cave + $1C teal bricks), 3 -> selector 4 $8D10 (castle grayscale). PROOF: with $075F=0, writing $0760=1 on the title and starting gave $074E=1/$074F=9 (an overworld-looking area at layout $A832); writing $0760=2 gave $074E=2/$074F=0/$0750=$C0 and World 1-2's black underground screen with layout pointer $00E7/$00E8=$AC37 (see the 'underground' scene). Death reloads do NOT re-run this selector - they reuse the latched $074E/$074F - so the write must happen before Start (or before the next-level transition), not on the WORLD x-y card.","confidence":1}}
